# damage resistance file for StuG III Ausf G (stug3g)
# correlates parts with equivelant armor thickness
# when hit, a part will act like a homogeneous plate of specified
# thickness
#
#
# format:
# name,thickness,hardness1,hardness2,concussive resistance, damage threshold
#
# where "name" is the object name in the hitmap tree for the vehicle
# thickness is the thickness of homogeneous armor equivelant (std US class B type)
#   NOTE: thickness is in MILLIMETERS! not inches
# hardness1 is the face hardness (used for face hardness effects)
# hardness2 is the average hardness (w/o this parameter, or set to zero, treated as 
#    homogeneous armor
# 
# hardness is used to determine either face shatter or projectile breakup
# use brinnell values (values of zero should be used for non-hard objects
# like internals, where the odds of projectile breakup is very low

#sounds and stuff
-hitsound1 = sounds\hit1.wav
-hitsound2 = sounds\hit2.wav
-hitsound3 = sounds\hit3.wav
-shraphitsound1 = sounds\shraphit1.wav
-shraphitsound2 = sounds\shraphit2.wav
-shraphitsound3 = sounds\shraphit3.wav
-hitenergymaxvolume = 1000000

